      "verdict": "DISTINCT",
      "reason": "Both concern ordering around a rejection, and the independent audit flagged them as sharing one invariant and one blind spot. They are kept because the ordering is with respect to different things and is observed with different instruments: inventory-orientation-task is about whether a rejected adjustment reaches the repository persistence call saveItem at all, measured with a pass-through probe over the store, and additionally asks the solver to locate and reuse an existing repository invariant across modules. b2-partial-validation-mutation is about whether any property of a caller-owned in-memory object is written before validation completes, measured with a write-recording proxy, and its contract explicitly permits mutating that object once validation has succeeded - a permitted path inventory-orientation-task has no analogue for."
